":"2025-10-13T17:54:30Z","closed_at":"2025-10-13T17:37:12Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nTested in:\n\n- 4.3 stable\n- 4.4 stable\n- 4.5 stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7688) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-12700K (20 threads) - 31.76 GiB memory\n\nTested with a Valve Index with SteamVR.\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen viewed in VR, shaders which use `CAMERA_VISIBLE_LAYERS` to change their rendering based on the camera's cull mask look incorrect. It seems that CAMERA_VISIBLE_LAYERS is always set to the default value, where all layers are active, in VR.\n\nFor example, with a VR camera that only has the first layer (bit 0) set, this shader produces red, although it should produce blue (since bit 1 == 2^1 == 2 is not set):\n\n```\nvoid fragment() {\n\tif ((int(CAMERA_VISIBLE_LAYERS) & 2) == 2) {\n\t\tALBEDO = vec3(1.0, 0.0, 0.0);\n\t} else {\n\t\tALBEDO = vec3(0.0, 0.0, 1.0);\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nOn the other hand, setting the object's render layers via the UI for entirely hiding objects does work as expected for VR cameras. This seems to only affect the `CAMERA_VISIBLE_LAYERS`  shader parameter.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun the MRP (which contains the shader shown above) with a VR headset and observe that the normal camera shows a blue cube, while the VR camera with the same cull mask displays a red cube. Both cameras correctly hide the other cube.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[vr-render-layer-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22883490/vr-render-layer-bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111585/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111585/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}